At present I think it reasonable to presume that natlangs do have clearly
specified rules, which is why we can speak them, especially when learnt
from birth. For Lojban there are no rules mapping 7 vowel phonemes to
vowel space, and all that constrains any arbitrary mapping is the need
to be understood.

